.TH CBMAP_REMOVE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_remove \- remove a key-value pair (type-inferred)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cbstmap.h>

ccol_retval_t cbmap_remove(hm_name, key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-inferred wrapper for cbmap_delete_elem() that returns its result
code. The tree is rebalanced after the delete.

The lookup key is converted through the DECLARED key type of the tree,
as cbmap_insert(3) converts it, so a key stored through that conversion
is found again only by a lookup that makes the same conversion. Both a
literal and a computed expression are accepted.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name  BST map to remove from
key      Key to remove
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success if the key was removed.
ccol_key_not_found if the key is not in the map.
ccol_invalid_args if key is a NULL character pointer, which is not a
string.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
ccol_key_not_found doesn't stop the program. The memory of the removed key
and value is freed.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_delete_elem (3),
.BR cbmap_insert (3)
